# LF everywhere, on every checkout (D6).
#
# The Content-Security-Policy carries SHA-256 hashes of the page's inline
# <script> and <style>, and a hash covers exact bytes. This workstation has
# core.autocrlf=true, so without this line a Windows checkout would hold CRLF
# while the image built in CI holds LF, and the header built from one would
# refuse the page served from the other.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.woff2 binary
*.png binary
